{title: 522 - My Hope Is Built on Nothing Less}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #522 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 522}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]My hope [F]is built on nothing less [C]than Jesus' blood [F]and righteousness.
[Bb]I dare [C]not trust [F]the [C]sweetest [F]frame, but wholly [C]lean on [F]Jesus' [Bb]name.
[Bb]On Christ the solid [C]rock I [F]stand; all other ground is sinking sand,
[Bb]All other ground is sinking [F]sand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F]On Christ the solid rock I [C]stand;
[C]all other [F]ground is [Bb]sinking [F]sand,
[C]all other ground is sinking [F]sand.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]When [F]Darkness veils his [C]lovely [Bb]face,
[Bb]I [C]rest [F]on his unchanging [Bb]grace.
[Bb]in every [F]high and stormy gale,
[Bb]my anchor holds within [F]the veil.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]His [F]oath, his covenant, his [Bb]blood
[Bb]supports [F]me in the [C]whelming [Bb]flood.
[Bb]When all [C]around [F]my soul gives way,
[Bb]he then is all my hope [F]and stay.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]When [F]He shall come [C]with trumpet [Bb]sound,
[Bb]O [C]may [F]I then in [C]him be [Bb]found!
[Bb]Dressed in [C]his righteousness [F]alone,
[Bb]faultless to stand before [F]the throne.
{end_of_verse}
